#: ../../source/docs/common-px4fmu-overview.rst:217
#: b87cf286f68b425aaad160f5b21a2fc5
msgid "**Wire the PX4-IO board.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4fmu-overview.rst:219
#: 8131562353d24ebabac517c2f50e2762
msgid "The PX4IO board has a built in Power Supply which can connect to up to 18 volts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4fmu-overview.rst:221
#: 1b743de5283c4a9b881549405e49ccf8
msgid "Insert the white PAP-02-VS 2 pin connector with the black and red wires coming out of it into the mating power connector you soldered in previously on the PX4IO board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4fmu-overview.rst:224
#: a3e11f4e811d455a98968ad576423749
msgid "Battery Plus is the(red wire) and should be soldered to your battery red power lead / connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4fmu-overview.rst:226
#: b11b9e78e5514caf95325b059e6c65bf
msgid "Battery Ground is the(black wire) and should be soldered to your battery black battery (Ground) lead / connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4fmu-overview.rst:229
#: 975b9e927f974ef4817ba5f60deb0596
msgid "**The main power inputs of your ESC's will also need to connect to these wires and to a battery connector.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4fmu-overview.rst:232
#: 2b09b3e6cca14322bf490c80157e3abf
msgid "A Power Distribution board can also be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4fmu-overview.rst:234
#: 456195b011e646feac3fbf3da839c802
msgid "**Connect your PPM-Sum RC receiver's 3 wire cable to the end of the 9 x 3 angle connector that is nearest the edge of the PX4IO board with the signal wire furthest from the board and the ground closest to the board.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4fmu-overview.rst:238
#: 005cbaa5974a468a8889046fefddbaea
msgid "**Wire the PX4FMU boards servo out signals to your ESC control inputs.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4fmu-overview.rst:240
#: 930306c49cde46329485629cbd926c9a
msgid "Run the Signal wires ONLY from the ESCs to the 3 x 9 Servo Connector on the PX4IO board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4fmu-overview.rst:242
#: c5f9da8662fe4f1f886b2141db9db046
msgid "The PX4IO board connector for Motor 1 is at the edge of the connector next to the Battery power in wires."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4fmu-overview.rst:244
#: e9b6e6c8f9ce4dd7917871076b26a41e
msgid "Insert the Motor ESC wires arranged progressively from that edge, (1,2,3,4,etc) for 2 to 8 motors depending on your copter type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4fmu-overview.rst:246
#: 79a7593cecb24ab5bc3cc8b38c139528
msgid "You can put the ESC Signal wires into a single inline connector with the correct number of pins for your copter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4fmu-overview.rst:248
#: 030d54e4bebd4d65a2cddee43935666f
msgid "The ESC Signal Wires / connector should be plugged into the top row (furthest from the board) of the PX4IO boards 3 x 9 Servo Connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4fmu-overview.rst:252
#: 1bd95f43b0614b31a5a03f132c5618a5
msgid "**Note, the cable that is supplied in the plastic envelope with the UBLOX GPS which has white 6 pin connectors on both ends is not the correct cable for the PX4FMU board.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4fmu-overview.rst:256
#: adbfd2be25d44ade91c9c8cf445691bd
msgid "The correct longer GPS cable is provided in a separate envelope and has a 5 pin \"beige\" connector on one end and a 6 pin white connector on the other end."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4fmu-overview.rst:259
#: cc755f2945ea4965bde6569a797f6d8f
msgid "Plug the correct GPS cable's white 6 pin connector into the 6 pin socket on the GPS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4fmu-overview.rst:261
#: c99ab38ea0da4fa99f4d3df6c96c0e40
msgid "Plug the beige 5 pin connector into the PX4FMU board's 5 pin GPS socket which is next to the 15 pin DF13 Mini connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4fmu-overview.rst:264
#: 4cdaea820d2f4ef7aadf424e0e562901
msgid "**Plug the 2 pin connector attached to the lead supplied with the buzzer into the buzzer socket on the side of the PX4FMU board that has the SD card holder on it.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-px4fmu-overview.rst:267
#: 4514b99651da416394bb0288a512b577
msgid "**Connect the \"Arming Switch\" to the Arming switch connector on the PX4IO board on the opposite side of the board from the Battery pads.**"
msgstr ""
